<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     TIME DIFFERENCE MECHANICS SECTION
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section" id="time-difference" aria-labelledby="time-diff-heading">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Mathematical Mechanics</p>
    <h2 id="time-diff-heading">Understanding the 7-Hour EET to EST Offset</h2>
    <p>
      The mathematical offset between Eastern European Time and Eastern Standard Time is straightforward: <strong>EST is exactly 7 hours behind EET</strong>. In UTC terminology, EET corresponds to UTC+2, while EST corresponds to UTC-5. Calculating the time difference requires taking the EET value and subtracting 7 hours:
    </p>
    <p style="text-align: center; font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: bold; color: var(--accent); background: var(--panel); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--line);">
      EST Time = EET Time − 7 Hours
    </p>
    <p>
      If your calculation crosses backwards past midnight (00:00), the result lands on the previous calendar day. For instance, 4:00 AM EET on Tuesday corresponds to 9:00 PM EST on Monday evening.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- SIDE-BY-SIDE GRAPHIC -->
  <div style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 700px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px;">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 600 180" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
      <rect width="600" height="180" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
      
      <g transform="translate(120, 90)">
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="55" fill="#12455d" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="3" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-36" stroke="#f4fbff" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="25" y2="0" stroke="#8fd7ff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <text x="0" y="75" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="14" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">EET (UTC+2)</text>
      </g>

      <g transform="translate(300, 90)">
        <text x="0" y="8" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="28" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">→</text>
        <rect x="-45" y="-30" width="90" height="24" rx="12" fill="#1b536e" />
        <text x="0" y="-14" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="800" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">SUBTRACT 7 HRS</text>
      </g>

      <g transform="translate(480, 90)">
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="55" fill="#12455d" stroke="#2f6278" stroke-width="3" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="-25" y2="25" stroke="#bdd2dc" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-36" stroke="#f4fbff" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <text x="0" y="75" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="14" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">EST (UTC-5)</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>1. Subtraction Formula</h3>
      <p>Take the hour in EET and subtract 7. If the resulting number is negative, add 24 to get the hour in EST and move back one day on the calendar.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>2. Business Overlap Window</h3>
      <p>Because of the 7-hour gap, the standard European afternoon (3:00 PM – 6:00 PM EET) aligns with the US East Coast morning (8:00 AM – 11:00 AM EST).</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>3. Summer Synchronization</h3>
      <p>When Europe shifts to EEST (UTC+3) and the US shifts to EDT (UTC-4), both zones advance 1 hour simultaneously, maintaining the 7-hour gap for most of summer.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

