<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     DAYLIGHT SAVING TRANSITION INFOGRAPHIC & EXPLANATION
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="content-section" id="dst-explained">
  <h2>Daylight Saving Time (DST) Differences: EET/EEST vs EST/EDT</h2>
  <p>
    Both Eastern Europe and Eastern North America observe Daylight Saving Time, but their schedules transition on different dates in spring and autumn. This results in brief annual periods where the standard 7-hour difference expands or contracts.
  </p>

  <!-- SVG DST Diagram -->
  <div style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 750px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px;">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 700 200" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
      <rect width="700" height="200" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
      
      <!-- Winter Track -->
      <g transform="translate(30, 40)">
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="640" height="35" rx="6" fill="#12455d" stroke="#2f6278" />
        <text x="15" y="22" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#f4fbff">Winter (Standard Time):</text>
        <text x="220" y="22" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="#36c7b5">EET (UTC+2) vs EST (UTC-5)</text>
        <text x="540" y="22" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#8fd7ff">7 Hours Gap</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Summer Track -->
      <g transform="translate(30, 90)">
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="640" height="35" rx="6" fill="#12455d" stroke="#2f6278" />
        <text x="15" y="22" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#f4fbff">Summer (Daylight Time):</text>
        <text x="220" y="22" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="#36c7b5">EEST (UTC+3) vs EDT (UTC-4)</text>
        <text x="540" y="22" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#8fd7ff">7 Hours Gap</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Transition Anomaly Track -->
      <g transform="translate(30, 140)">
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="640" height="40" rx="6" fill="#1b536e" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="15" y="25" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#36c7b5">Spring/Fall Transition Weeks:</text>
        <text x="220" y="25" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#f4fbff">US shifts 2 weeks earlier in March / 1 week later in Nov</text>
        <text x="540" y="25" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#36c7b5">6 or 8 Hours Gap</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <p>
    In the United States, Daylight Saving Time begins on the second Sunday of March and ends on the first Sunday of November. In the European Union (including EET countries), Daylight Saving Time begins on the last Sunday of March and ends on the last Sunday of October. During the gap periods in March and late October/early November, the time difference temporarily becomes <strong>6 hours</strong> or <strong>8 hours</strong>.
  </p>
</section>

